---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Sale — Buzzyfly"
	description="Terms for buying Buzzyfly digital products, refunds, and license."
	pubDate={new Date('September 16 2026')}
>
	<p>Last updated: September 16, 2026</p>

	<p>
		These terms apply when you buy a product on buzzyfly.com. Questions: coachmanager@gmail.com.
	</p>

	<h2>What you are buying</h2>
	<p>
		Digital files (checklists, templates, and related documents). One-time payment. No subscription. No coaching calls. Lifetime access to the files plus future updates we choose to add to that product.
	</p>

	<h2>Delivery</h2>
	<p>
		After Stripe confirms payment, a private download link is sent to the email used at checkout. The link is time-limited. The files themselves are yours to keep. If the email does not arrive, write coachmanager@gmail.com from the checkout address.
	</p>

	<h2>Refunds</h2>
	<p>
		7-day email refund if the files are not what the store lists. Email coachmanager@gmail.com within 7 days of purchase. No extra hoops.
	</p>

	<h2>License</h2>
	<p>
		You may use the files in your own business. You may not resell, republish, or share the zip as a product. One purchase, one operator (or the team inside that operator's shop).
	</p>

	<h2>No guarantees beyond the files</h2>
	<p>
		Results depend on how you use the checklists. We do not promise revenue, client wins, or a specific number of hours saved.
	</p>

	<h2>Site and law</h2>
	<p>
		We can update these terms. The live page is the current version. If a court finds one line unenforceable, the rest still applies.
	</p>
</Layout>
